From 34fb430b45f6e4f8e68b85e60bac7407b322e38b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SIMD Audit <audit@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 14:06:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SIMD red-team audit: fix 6 miscompiles + 6 codegen/encoder
 defects, add regression tests

Auto-vectorizer (vectorize.rs):
- AVX2 matmul: byte limit (N/4)*32 (was N*8 => OOB write + dead remainder)
- SSE2 matmul remainder: width-aware start (IV*2, was IV/8)
- dot-product: scale BOTH array GEPs (break left B at scalar stride)
- matmul: require F64 element type (float matmul segfaulted)
- reduction cast-sum: reject cross-kind casts (float += int returned 0.0)

Backend:
- FmaF64x2: use regalloc assignments (B/C pointer aliasing)
- blendv256: result in ymm0 (returned the mask)
- horizontal-add SSE2: fix 3-operand unpckhpd/psrldq/paddd
- 256-bit unpack: add missing vunpcklps/hps/pd arms (were dropped)
- vhaddps/vhsubps/vaddsubps + FMA3 ss/sd: F2/F3 VEX prefix
- 128-bit vector copy width (was 256-bit vmovupd, clobbered locals)
- vpermilvarps/pd256: add builtin lowering + variable-form encoding
- encoder: remove 6 duplicate arms + fix vpcmpeq/vpcmpgt shadowing

Regression tests: 9 new self-checking tests (fail on pre-fix binary, match GCC);
run_regression.sh sources per-test .env for LCCC_FORCE_SSE2 coverage.

Validation: 12/12 SIMD reproducers match GCC; intrinsics 3/3; regression
120/120; correctness 50/50. zlib-ng adler32_avx2 correct (matches GCC +
zlib reference); instrs 963 vs gcc 674 / clang 504 => next win: vector
register allocation + memory-operand folding.
